    ... through a transit exchange                         2      1
  64 kbps data                                        cannot      0

  [tandem: 72 s]

FABRIC -- the highway cell by cell: 8 slots x 64 kHz = 512 kbps a block, up to 8 blocks.
  2048 frames a run, random data on every fitted port.

  1. Every source slot to every listening slot: 64 maps, port p listens to p+m (mod 64).
     4096 (source, listener) pairs, C and A: 0 bit errors at a delay of exactly 1 frame.

  2. Growth: random maps with 1 to 8 blocks fitted; an absent block or an empty slot is FILL / A=0.
      blocks  maps  bits checked  errors  listening to nothing
           1     8       2096128       0                   470
           2     8       2096128       0                   411
           3     8       2096128       0                   350
           4     8       2096128       0                   284
           5     8       2096128       0                   251
           6     8       2096128       0                   187
           7     8       2096128       0                   121
           8     8       2096128       0                    78

  3. Fan-out: 63 ports listen to port 25.
     all 64 received streams identical: True;  errors against the source: 0

  4. Idle: a cleared latch listens to port 00, which is never fitted.
     C_RX is FILL (1010): True;  A_RX is 0: True;  decoded level -48.3 dB re nominal speech

  5. Octets: a source sends bytes b0-first on TX_OCT; the listener frames on RX_OCT = TX_OCT + 1 frame.
     port 52 <- 31: 255 octets, 0 wrong
     port 07 <- 31: 255 octets, 0 wrong
     framed on TX_OCT instead (no delay allowed for): 253 of 255 wrong

  6. The marker re-points a latch at a random cell: 4000 writes.
     new source from the write frame on                                        2289
     old source for the write frame, then new                                  1045
     one bit held over (neither slot strobed in the write frame), then new      666
     anything else                                                                0
     accounted for: 4000 of 4000.  The worst a re-point does is repeat one bit: the slip of mf8-backplane.md 7.

  7. A trunk block: six ports on slots 1,2,3,5,6,7 of highway 1 are an MF8 frame (mf8.build / mf8.framer).
     clean                                frames delivered  8153 of 8192, re-frames 0; bits wrong on their own port 0; against a neighbour's source 50 %; far fabric errors 0
     one line bit slipped at frame 3000   frames delivered  8105 of 8191, re-frames 1; bits wrong on their own port 45 (all in frames 3000-3014, before the framer let go); against a neighbour's source 50 %; far fabric errors 0
     A through the S bit, clean line: 0 errors in 6114 samples

  8. A tie block: highway 7 of group X crossed to highway 7 of group Y, same clock, no framer.
     8 junctors, C and A: 0 errors at a delay of exactly 2 frames (one per fabric)

  [fabric: 41 s]

CALLS -- one exchange, one 1 kHz tick at a time.  Ports are dialled in octal, 00-77.
  00 idle (never fitted), 01 dial tone, 02 cannot-complete tone, 03-05 registers; subscribers 20-77.
  Release: M or E low for 256 ms (each port's two detectors +-20%), after 16 ms high.  Scanner: 8 ports a tick.

