MONITOR -- which rules keep a live flood from ever claiming a wrong number.
  A chain: an origin and 7 exchanges whose exchange digits are 1..7.  A dial at 10 pps +-10 %, 60/40; the
  trigger digit, the exchange digit (1-7, or ten pulses for an exchange that is not there) and one more.
  The origin seizes 130 ms after the trigger's last pulse; each exchange patches the seizure onward 3-10 ms
  after its M rises; A crosses every hop through the trunk's A path (aline 1).  A claim cuts the onward patch.
  1500 calls a row.  FALSE = an exchange other than the one dialled claimed the call.

