            2 ms    60 ms |      70.5        29.5      0 |  128 ms      0      15 %      0       0 %
            5 ms    80 ms |      72.8        27.2      0 |  128 ms      0      16 %      0       0 %
           10 ms   116 ms |      72.8        27.2      0 |  128 ms      0      16 %      0       0 %
           20 ms   186 ms |      73.1        26.8      1 |  256 ms      0      32 %      0       0 %
           40 ms   326 ms |      66.5        31.2     23 |  512 ms      0      69 %      0       0 %

  The guard must be at least the spread or it is not a guarantee, and no more than the
  caller's own pause less the 130 ms the digit and the seizure take.  A phone to
  ES 201 187 gives at least 720 ms (register.md 2), so the guard may go to 590 ms -- the
  512 ms tap, four taps up from 128 on the counter it already has.  At 7 hops that is
  67 ms a hop of wander against the present tap's 12.  It is free in parts and it costs
  the callers who dial faster than the tap allows: every one of those gets cannot-complete.

