TIMING -- the fabric in nanoseconds.  512 kbps: a cell is 1953 ns, HCLK high for its first half.
  Every delay in every trial drawn on its own between 0.35 x typical and the data-sheet maximum
  (74HC, 4.5 V, -40..85 C); 400000 trials; the figure is the WORST seen.  Times from the start of the cell.

  1. A highway bit at a listener's capture flip-flop: card or RBT mux -> commutator -> driver -> mainboard
     -> the listening block's receiver -> the port's highway select.
       valid by    252 ns        (typical 165)

  2. The capture clock: a '138 enabled while HCLK is low, addressed by the slot count DELAYED A QUARTER
     CELL, so its address only ever moves while it is disabled; the port's '151 picks one line, W clocks.
       address settled    368 ns before the enable, and moves    415 ns after the disable
       capture clock rises at    994 - 1099 ns
       set-up at the flip-flop    752 ns;  hold    927 ns

  3. The same decoder addressed by the count as it stands: at the turn of the cell the new address can
     arrive before the disable does, and the NEXT port's line pulses low with nothing settled.
       in 9.6 % of trials; wider than 8 ns in 4.4 %; worst 45 ns.  Typical parts: -18 ns, no pulse.
       It is only a hazard across the spread, which is exactly the kind not to build on.

  4. No re-timing flip-flop.  Every capture is at the middle of some cell, so nothing a card is given
     changes within half a cell of the frame edge, where every card samples (RX_CLK = TX_CLK here).
       a source in slot 7: C_RX settled    820 ns before the card samples
       a source in slot 0: C_RX moves      979 ns after it
     A bit sent in frame f is sampled at the edge that begins f+1 whatever the two slots: one frame,
     as `fabric` 1 measured, which already models the card as sampling at that edge.

  5. The economy form: C in the first half of the cell and A in the second on ONE highway wire, captured
     on the two edges of a strobe that is high for the middle half (the '151 gives both senses).
       C: set-up    256 ns, hold    390 ns;   A: set-up    293 ns, hold    423 ns

