SS0 -- the number on a common channel: one SEIZE a link, forward only; A carries everything else.
  Arithmetic from the constants of `flood`, not a simulation of the gates:
    a message is 18 bits at 1000 baud, 18 ms, and waits up to 1 ms for the TICK;
    a hop hunts onward in 5 ms (a flood hop, 7 ms, less its A path) and writes in 2 ms:
    26 ms a hop.  Register ID 128 ms; A rise 1.5 ms and fall 2.0 ms a hop; release 256 ms.

