TOPO -- what shapes of network the protocol carries, and how large.  A line makes 3 calls an hour of
  48 s; every call that leaves floods every link for 2.0 to 3.8 s by the code it calls, 2.73 s over all 64
  (exch-network.md 4); each shape is worked with its own codes, the backbone's from 00-17.  An exchange
  faces four directions at most and fits eight trunk groups at most; it keeps 48 lines with two
  groups and gives up six for each one more.  Arithmetic is Erlang B on a tree, as exch-network.md 5
  and `net` agree it may be; "pair" is the worst end-to-end loss between two exchanges, "lost" the mean.

