     late and not a call lost (exch-marker.md 6).  42 herds were let loose.

     A BURST DOES NOT OFFER THE SAME CALLS, and that is not the model being wrong.  The
     cold rate is set so the mean over the cycle is the smooth one, which is exact for
     arrivals out of nowhere; but a line that is off hook cannot lift, and at 8x the rate the
     hot idle is shorter than a call, so the lines themselves are the limit.  `net`, whose
     callers arrive from nowhere, cannot show this: it is what makes a line a source.
     "E a call/s" is the link's erlangs divided by the calls a second that produced them,
     so the three may be read against each other at the load each one managed to offer.

