BIG -- how near sixty-four exchanges the pulse flood will go, and what shape gets there.
  The rules are Topology.md 1: four directions an exchange, eight trunk groups, the flood
  sees a tree, sixty-four codes, and the whole flood inside the origin's 128 ms guard at a
  slow marker (12 ms a hop and 4 more at a hub).  Erlang B on a tree throughout,
  3 calls an hour of 48 s a line, and every call that leaves floods every link for
  2.73 s on average over the sixty-four codes.  "lines" is what the shape is worked at, after
  the trunk groups have taken their slots and the cap in the label has taken the rest.

  1. A tandem-chain backbone with spokes on it.  A tandem in the MIDDLE of the chain has
     two directions left after the backbone and two trunk groups, so it carries two spokes
     of six channels or one of twelve; an end of the chain has three directions and four
     groups.  That asymmetry is the whole of what a backbone costs.
