  4. FULLY CONNECTED tandems.  Of the k(k-1)/2 links between k tandems only the k-1 of a
     chain may carry the flood, because the flood must see a tree; every other one is
     STRAPPED, and a strapped link carries calls between its own two ends only
     (exch-network.md 3.3).  A tandem has twelve lines.  So this is what they are worth:
     Read the pairs: each is the SAME eight trunk groups at each tandem, spent on a chain
     of wide links or on a mesh of narrow ones.
