  7. What the GUARD'S TAP buys.  The flood has to cross the network inside the origin's
     guard (exch-monitor.md 3, rule 2), which is one tap on a counter -- 128 ms today, and
     12 ms a hop at a slow marker with 4 more at a hub.  It may go as far as the caller's
     own pause less the 130 ms the digit and the seizure take: a phone to ES 201 187 gives
     720 ms (register.md 2), so 590 ms, and 512 is the last tap under it.  A carrier's own
     delay is NOT in this budget (exch-monitor.md 5.1); wander is.

