    512ms     42         43   the guard |    64   1428    22   5.60 E on 12  0.74%    9 hp  140 ms
     "hops" is the longest chain whose flood fits the tap, whatever it would carry -- the
     timer alone.  The network beside it has both constraints on, and past 128 ms the guard
     stops being the one that binds: what stops the search then is the traffic on the
     centre and the four directions an exchange has, neither of which is a timer.

  8. Those run call by call with `net`'s engine -- the flood, the monitors, the claim, the
     resolvers and the registers -- five monitor cells a block and five resolvers a hub,
     at the busy hour of 3 calls a line and then at TWICE it, which is a network built for
